======================================================================
DEEP NUMEROLOGY: 25, 8, AND THE k-PERIODICITY PRINCIPLE
======================================================================

  The ratio D_graph(8) / D_tournament(8) = 19504 / 784 = 24.877551
  This is 1219/49 = 1219/49
  Reduced: 1219 / 49
  = 1219/49 = 24.877551

  Why the ratio is ~25:

  The number 8 = 2^3:
  2 = min_cycle of graphs
  3 = min_cycle of tournaments
  8 = 2^3 = product-as-power of the two min_cycles
  8 is also where the prime filter first makes no difference
  (all partitions up to n=8 have only prime parts)

  ============================================================
  2^10 = 1024 = 10^3 + 4! = 1000 + 24
  ============================================================
  2^10 = 1024
  10^3 = 1000
  4! = 24
  10^3 + 4! = 1024
  Match: True

  Tournament interpretation:
  At n=5: m = C(5,2) = 10
  Number of labeled tournaments on 5 vertices = 2^10 = 1024
  = 10^3 + 4! = 1000 + 24
  = m^3 + (n-1)! 
  Check: m^3 = 10^3 = 1000, (n-1)! = 4! = 24. Sum = 1024 = 2^m. ✓

